                <pb facs="0503" n="493" sameAs="frus:frus1937v05/pg493"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.2231/130: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Ecuador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gonzalez</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Quito</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-03-20T12:00:00-05:00">March 20,
                        1937—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 5:43 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>17. Referring to Department’s telegram No. 11, March 19, 6 p.m., the publication
                    of the list should be withheld until I obtain acquiescence on the part thereof
                    relating to bindings which is now being considered by the Department of
                    Finance.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gonzalez</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
